<section image-layout="blank" id="BblFLMzy0S" background-color="heading"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="wLbH1828G7" vertical-align="center" colspan="36"><p role="eyebrow">Ozone policy · Investment committee · 23 Sep 2026</p><h1 font-size="46pt">Map the machinery before you price the risk</h1><p font-size="lg">Proposed diligence thesis: exposure sits in substance-dependent equipment and lifecycle obligations—not in broad sector labels. Separate legacy ozone-depleting substances from HFC climate exposure; validate the asset inventory; then price timing, capex and operating resilience.</p><spacer size="20pt"></spacer><hr color="accent" thickness="md" width="xs"><p font-size="16pt"><b>Screening perimeter:</b> refrigeration · HVAC · foam · fire suppression · industrial processes</p></grid-item><grid-item id="YjKjeNyR-t" padding="0" colspan="24"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/wHnkhVXJiuFksl97P2xAz.png" saved-media-id="cupvvlggk7n080u" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="industrial-atmospheric-relief" alt="Precision editorial relief construction of atmospheric layers intersecting with a refrigeration compressor, cooling coil, recovery cylinder and valves, built from matte mineral paper and oxidized metal under cool raking studio light, exposure blue, transition teal, restrained rust accents and charcoal shadows, no text, no lettering, no logos" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="frvsxtIFzF" background-color="heading" padding="12pt 16pt"><p font-size="14pt">Conceptual equipment relief · cooling compressor, coil, cylinder and valves · not portfolio assets</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>